@startuml HTTP Request Lifecycle
!theme plain
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam backgroundColor #F5F5F5
skinparam defaultFontSize 11

title NestJS HTTP Request - Complete Processing Pipeline

participant "HTTP Client" as CLIENT
participant "Express/Fastify" as ADAPTER
participant "Middleware" as MIDDLEWARE
participant "GuardsConsumer" as GUARDS
participant "PipesConsumer" as PIPES
participant "InterceptorsConsumer" as INTERCEPTORS
participant "Route Handler" as HANDLER
participant "ExceptionFilters" as FILTERS
participant "Response" as RESP

CLIENT ->> ADAPTER: HTTP Request\n(GET /users/1)
activate ADAPTER

ADAPTER ->> MIDDLEWARE: execute(request, response, next)
activate MIDDLEWARE
MIDDLEWARE ->> ADAPTER: next() → continue
deactivate MIDDLEWARE

ADAPTER ->> GUARDS: canActivate(context)
activate GUARDS
note right of GUARDS
    Check:
    - @UseGuards(AuthGuard)
    - @UseGuards(RoleGuard)
    - Scoped & Global guards
end note

alt Guard Fails
    GUARDS ->> FILTERS: throw UnauthorizedException
else Guard Passes
    GUARDS ->> ADAPTER: return true
    deactivate GUARDS

    ADAPTER ->> PIPES: transform(value, metadata)
    activate PIPES
    note right of PIPES
        Apply:
        - @Param('id', ParseIntPipe)
        - @Body(ValidationPipe)
        - Custom pipes
        - Transform/Validate data
    end note
    PIPES ->> ADAPTER: transformed value
    deactivate PIPES

    ADAPTER ->> INTERCEPTORS: intercept(context, next)
    activate INTERCEPTORS
    note right of INTERCEPTORS
        Before Handler:
        - Logging
        - Performance tracking
        - Data transformation
    end note

    INTERCEPTORS ->> HANDLER: next.handle()
    activate HANDLER
    note right of HANDLER
        Execute route handler:
        @Get(':id')
        getUser(id: number)
    end note

    HANDLER ->> HANDLER: Handler logic
    HANDLER -->> INTERCEPTORS: Observable<Response>
    deactivate HANDLER

    note right of INTERCEPTORS
        After Handler:
        - Transform response
        - Add headers
        - Serialize data
    end note
    INTERCEPTORS ->> ADAPTER: response
    deactivate INTERCEPTORS

    ADAPTER ->> RESP: send(response)
end

FILTERS ->> RESP: error response
deactivate FILTERS

RESP ->> CLIENT: HTTP Response\n(200 / 4xx / 5xx)
deactivate ADAPTER

note over CLIENT, RESP
    Exception Handling:
    1. Any exception caught
    2. Find matching @Catch filter
    3. Filter determines response
    4. Send error response
end note

@enduml
